# Semantic Search with OpenAI and Typesense
created: undefined, last updated: 2026-08-09, [Read more](https://typesense.org/docs/guide/semantic-search.html)

## # Step 2: Index your JSON data
You can send your JSON data as usual into Typesense:
```
curl "http://localhost:8108/collections/products/documents/import?action=create" \
-H "X-TYPESENSE-API-KEY: ${TYPESENSE_API_KEY}" \
-H "Content-Type: text/plain" \
-X POST \
-d '{"product_name": "Cell phone"}
{"product_name": "Laptop"}
{"product_name": "Desktop"}
{"product_name": "Printer"}
{"product_name": "Keyboard"}
{"product_name": "Monitor"}
{"product_name": "Mouse"}'
```
Typesense will automatically use the ML model you specified when creating the schema to generate and store embeddings for each of your JSON documents.

# Mastering Typesense: Efficient Document Management and Real ...
created: 2024-09-02, last updated: 2026-05-16, [Read more](https://medium.com/@prabha.ochetty/mastering-typesense-efficient-document-management-and-real-time-search-integration-885c1ce1b3f3)

public function addDocument()
...
// Convert the document data to JSON
$jsonData = json_encode($documentData);
// Initialize cURL
$ch = curl_init();
// Set cURL options
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_URL, $typesenseHost . '/collections/books/documents');
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, 1);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POST, 1);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS, $jsonData);
// Set Headers
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER, [
'Content-Type: application/json',
'X-TYPESENSE-API-KEY: ' . $apiKey
]);
// Execute the request
$response = curl_exec($ch);
...
> **Note**: Typesense also supports importing data via files.
Before you import these files the data should be converted to JSON format.

